| 8 | 3 | Dance steps. *How do steps become a phrase, and how do two dances from different places use the beat?* | 8 | g3-dance-steps | | Cues: "listen, count to four, step on the beat". Settings: a longways line with a partner, a circle | Dance steps strung into short four-count phrases in two dance styles, in a line, a circle and with a partner: begun toward SHAPE.S1.5.1 (owned in grade 4, unit 13) and SHAPE.S1.5.5 (owned in grade 4, unit 15). Picks: the Virginia Reel, a longways dance done in the United States since the 1800s from English and Irish country dance roots (the line-dance style), and Alunelul, a Romanian children's song and stamping dance done in a line or circle (the folk style), neither used in K to 2. Opens with a retrieval task on K to 2 grade 2 unit 21's three-move sequence. Ends: 1 check day (skill task: a four-count pattern to the beat in each dance; knowledge task: says one way the two dances differ in formation or step; conduct: kind to a partner in the line, S3.5.3 review), 1 respond day. Tools: music track or the teacher's drum; Curio Class writes the dance cards and each dance's short source line | Last in grade 3 so its phrases hand straight to grade 4's chains and dance sequences; dance returns every year of the band (units 8, 15, 22), never taught once and dropped; after the year-end check because the core checks hold weeks 28 to 32 | Candidate: partners teach each other one phrase | Cultural content: US country dance and Romanian folk traditions; partners set by the teacher with no gender roles (the Virginia Reel is often taught in lines split by gender: here it is not); no costume or imitation of a people. Communities: US traditional dance and Romanian. Spot-checked 2026-11-25: the Virginia Reel in an encyclopedia entry and a Library of Congress record of an 1800s dance manual that covers it (loc.gov/item/afcreed000072, catalog record); Alunelul at a folk dance notes archive (folkdancefootnotes.org, "Alunelu(l), children's song and dance, Romania"); the agent studies a national folklife archive's entry and a Romanian cultural institution's page first. Swap allowed (Swaps). Cost: $0 |
