## Course-level checks

Each check samples earlier units by skill tasks (the main cue of a sampled unit at a new station or in a new
setting), short knowledge tasks shown by moving, said to the teacher or written in one line, and conduct watched again
at the new station or carried unscored. A child is watched once in each window. Across a year's two checks every
standard (S1 to S4) is sampled at least once from units before the check. The weeks avoid the weeks where
docs/courses/CALENDAR.md holds a core check for that grade (grade 3: 9, 12, 14, 16, 20, 23, 25, 28, 30, 31, 32;
grade 4: 8, 9, 10, 12, 16, 19, 21, 23, 27, 30, 31, 32; grade 5: 10, 11, 16, 17, 21, 22, 29, 30, 31, 32). Every year
uses the same days: mid-year check days 43 and 44 with the respond day 45 (all week 18), year-end check days 63 and
64 with the respond day 65 (all week 26), so respond days fall in free weeks too. Clashes with other after-core
courses' checks wait on the lead's calendar pass across all after-core frames (For the lead 5).

| Check | After unit | Check days | Respond days | What it checks |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Grade 3 mid-year (week 18, course days 43 and 44 of the year) | 4 | 2 | 1 | Units 1 to 3, at new stations: a change of direction into open space (unit 1), three throws to a target and catches at two heights (unit 2), a soft landing and a balance (unit 3); knowledge: when a warm-up is needed (unit 1) and the key parts of the throw (unit 2); conduct: stays safe with no reminder (unit 1, S3). Unit 4's record (taken days before) is carried unscored. Respond on day 45 |
