## For the lead

1. **Pattern copied from the K to 2 pilot.** One file with a Year column, each year whole; every year ends on short
   units after its year-end check (week 26), because K to 5 weeks 28 to 32 are mostly core check weeks; each unit's
   Ends names one skill task, one knowledge task and one S3 behavior; across a year's two checks every standard is
   sampled from units before the check; the short path is computed from this band's own dose. Dose kept at the
   APPROACH default (80 x 35).
2. **Check weeks, one pattern for all three years.** Mid-year days 43 to 45 (week 18) and year-end days 63 to 65
   (week 26) are off every core check week of grades 3, 4 and 5, respond days included, so the K to 2 frame's
   respond-day question (its For the lead 5) does not arise here.
3. **C3 column header.** As the pilot's For the lead 3: PE uses it for cues and settings. Pick: rename it "Cues and
   settings" for PE in frame-write.md item 5 and in frame.py's reader, if it reads the header.
4. **Row note (Row changes).** g5-goal's cross_subject lean is on 5.G.A.2, which math grade 5 teaches in weeks 27 to
   30; the goal unit runs in weeks 1 to 6 because a four- to six-week goal needs the year's open weeks. Pick: keep
   the lean for the grade 6 return and add the bar-graph fallback to the row's note (Row changes).
5. **After-core check clashes, for the lead's calendar pass.** PE uses week 18 and week 26 in grades 3, 4 and 5; the
   other after-core 3 to 5 frames are being written now, so the clash list waits on that pass. PE's free
   alternatives off core weeks: grade 3 weeks 17, 18, 19, 26, 27 and 29; grade 4 weeks 17, 18, 20, 22, 24, 25, 26,
   28, 29; grade 5 weeks 18, 19, 20, 23 to 28.
6. **Health 3 to 5 and SEL 3 to 5 sides.** The health frame landed while this one was written; its units are cited in
   Cross-subject. Pick: health unit 15 (g5-pa-habit-practice) and PE unit 17 run in the same weeks, so health's log
   tracks the PE goal as its activity habit (one log, not two); health's frame does not say so yet. SEL's calm-down
   unit names PE unit 6 when it lands. Dance 3 to 5 places its rows against PE units 8, 15 and 22.
7. **Cultural picks to confirm.** Virginia Reel, Alunelul, La Bastringue, jianzi and tinikling were spot-checked at
   encyclopedia, folk dance archive, university and national archive pages only (2026-11-25); none was confirmed at a
   community's own institution in this pass, which is the sensitivity agent's first task (no download or sign-in
   needed). The line dance in unit 15 is written by Curio Class and claims no culture.

## For Cory

- Money: the band's provisional new buys are about $390 for a school with only the K to 2 closet (pinnies, hoops,
  kicking and dribble balls, rackets, trainer balls, two low nets, ribbons, shuttlecocks, bases). Is the per-year PE
  equipment ceiling of $150 (asked in the K to 2 fix report) right for grades 3 to 5 too? Grade 3 needs about $220
  of it.

