 succeeded in 351ms:
g3-jump-land-balance | SHAPE.S1.5.7; SHAPE.S1.5.8 | assumes g2-travel-jump-balance | Jump and land while staying in place (two feet, one foot, a half turn) and balance on different body parts, including a partner balance at a safe size. Cues: bend, swing, land soft, hold. Boundary: in place, stable surfaces. Assessed by a skill task: lands three jumps softly and holds two balances for three counts. Teacher note: soft floor or mats; partner balances stay low.
g3-body-roll | SHAPE.S1.5.3 | assumes g2-travel-jump-balance | Body rolls in a fixed spot on a mat: log roll, egg roll, and a forward roll down an incline for children who are ready. Cues: tuck chin, round back, hands on the mat. Assessed by a skill task: one roll watched against two cues; rolls that need more tries are adapted, not skipped. Teacher note: mats; no rolling for a child with a neck or back concern from a family or nurse; a log roll is always the alternative.
g3-rope | SHAPE.S1.5.6 | assumes g2-rope-fixed | Jump rope through several tasks: self-turned forward and backward, with a step and a jump, a long rope with a turner, a partner rope. Cues: small jumps, turn from the wrists, steady beat. Assessed by a skill task: ten jumps in a row at the child's own pace; growth is measured against the child's own start. Teacher note: adapted ropes for a range of ability.
g3-throw-roll-catch | SHAPE.S1.5.9; SHAPE.S1.5.10; SHAPE.S1.5.12; ~SHAPE.S1.5.17 | assumes g2-overhand-throw; g2-ball-skills-combine | Roll from a fixed spot (a ball to a target), throw overhand and underhand in several tasks (to a wall, a hoop, a partner), and catch at several heights. Cues: step, throw, follow through; hands out, eyes on it, soft hands. Passing with the hands to a moving partner is owned in grade 4. Assessed by a skill task: throws three of five to a target at a set distance with the cues, catches three of five tosses. Teacher note: one throwing direction; no human targets.
g3-strike-tools | SHAPE.S1.5.11; SHAPE.S1.5.16 | assumes g2-long-strike; g2-ball-skills-combine | Hit with a long-handled tool (bat, hockey stick) and a short-handled tool (paddle, racket) in several tasks: off a tee, a toss to oneself, a gentle toss from a partner. Cues: side to the target, eyes on the ball, swing through. Assessed by a skill task: contacts a gently tossed ball three of five times with a swing through. Teacher note: swing space cleared; one batter per space; line behind a safe distance.
g3-foot-skills | SHAPE.S1.5.18; SHAPE.S1.5.20 | assumes g2-ball-skills-combine | Kick with the laces to a target and to a partner and dribble with the feet in open space, changing direction. Cues: plant foot beside the ball, laces through the ball, small taps. Assessed by a skill task: kicks a rolled ball to a partner and dribbles through five cones without bumping. Teacher note: kicks aimed at a wall or goal, never at a person.
g3-hand-dribble | SHAPE.S1.5.19 | assumes g2-ball-skills-combine | Bounce a ball with the hands in place and on the move with one hand, then with a changed hand. Cues: push, fingers wide, eyes up. Boundary: dribbling with the ball while changing direction against defenders is later. Assessed by a skill task: dribbles ten steps without losing the ball.
g3-dance-steps | ~SHAPE.S1.5.1; ~SHAPE.S1.5.5 | assumes g2-dance-sequence | Dance steps strung into short phrases in two dance styles (a folk dance, a line dance): four-count patterns in a line, a circle or with a partner. Works toward the traveling chain and the dance sequence owned in grade 4. Assessed by a skill task: performs a four-count pattern to the beat. Each cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it. Sacred or ceremonial activities: APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground.
g3-safe-movement | SHAPE.S2.5.1 | assumes g2-chase-flee; g2-show-ideas | Use movement ideas and tactics to stay safe where the setting keeps changing: scan the room, keep eyes up, choose open space, change direction, use the safe-space bubble. Practiced in small dodge and tag games with no elimination. Assessed by a knowledge task: names a safe move when the setting changes.
