18 | 2 | 10 | g2-rope-fixed; g2-foods-energy | SHAPE.S1.2.16; SHAPE.S2.2.11 | Jump a self-turned rope in a fixed spot, once and then several in a row, or a long rope with a turner (S1.2.16, owned here; tried in K and grade 1). Foods for energy open with a retrieval task on health K to 2 unit 12's energy-snack sort (grade 2 weeks 1 to 5), where health teaches foods that give energy for play; PE teaches its own part: choosing what to eat and drink before and while playing, and water as the drink for moving, with the water break taken on the rope days (S2.2.11). Opens also with a retrieval task on grade 1 unit 9's rope swings. Ends: 1 check day (skill task: three self-turned jumps in a row or one long-rope jump; knowledge prompt: pick a snack and a drink for before playing from picture cards and say what to drink while playing; conduct: ropes kept in the rope space and coiled back, S3.2.7 review), 1 respond day. Tools: ropes matched to height; food picture cards from foods a class commonly sees (ours) | Before the mid-year check: rope needs grade 1's jump and landing and the rhythm of unit 15's sequences; foods for energy sits with rope because rope is the year's most tiring skill, so choosing food and water for play is real
