| cue-words | Not new: PE K to 2 unit 1 (k-jump-land), carried through 3 to 5 | Unit 1: a skill said in two or three short cue words, the base that skill analysis builds on | Units 1 to 7 (model_in of the grade 6 motor rows); afterward carried inside skill-analysis |
| skill-analysis | New (g6-analyze-skill, model_out) | Unit 1: preparation, action, follow through; watch a partner with the cue card and name the part to fix and its cue. Taught on the first skill days, before any other row uses it | Every later unit (model_in of every motor row from unit 1's throw on): 2 to 22; goes on to grade 9 |
| tactics-question | Not new: PE K to 2 unit 20 (g2-chase-flee), carried through 3 to 5 | Unit 4 (g6-pass-receive): where is the space, and what is my best move? | Units 5, 7, 8, 9, 11, 12, 16, 17, 19; goes on to grade 9 |
| fitt-plan | Not new: PE grade 5 (g5-fitt) | Unit 2 (g6-skill-fitness-technique, g6-stretch-types): frequency, intensity, time and type | Units 3, 10, 14, 15, 18; goes on to grade 9 |
| fitness-parts | Not new: PE grade 3 (g3-health-fitness) | Unit 2 (g6-fitness-parts): health-related and skill-related parts | Units 3, 10, 15; goes on to grade 9 |
